namespace App\Support;

/**
 * The assistant widget's icons, as paths rather than as a font.
 *
 * They were Bootstrap-icons glyphs, which meant the widget only drew
 * correctly on the pages that load `app.scss`. On the homepage — a different
 * stylesheet entirely — the launcher showed an empty square where the star
 * belongs. Importing the whole icon font into that bundle did fix it, and
 * cost eighty kilobytes of CSS to draw four glyphs.
 *
 * These are lifted verbatim from the same `bootstrap-icons` package by a
 * script, so nothing is drawn by hand and nothing can drift from what the
 * admin preview shows. Every name the widget can be configured with is here:
 * the seven the launcher offers, the three its own controls use, and every
 * icon a quick action can carry.
 *
 * `path()` falls back to the sparkle. The stored value is validated as
 * `bi-*` rather than against this list, and a button with nothing in it is
 * worse than a button with the default.
 */
